        "title": "Base-chat spawns context-pruner before each step",
        "summary": "The `base-chat` conversational agent gains a `handleSteps` generator that spawns the `context-pruner` subagent inline before every step, sizing the prune budget to the model this step will use. It computes `maxContextLength` as floor(window * 0.4) from an inline `CONTEXT_WINDOWS` map that mirrors the exported `FREEBUFF_MODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOWS` table in `common/src/constants/freebuff-models.ts`, falling back to `FREEBUFF_DEFAULT_CONTEXT_WINDOW` (131072) for unmeasured models. The runtime now passes `model: template.model` into the handleSteps invocation context, and `AgentStepContext` plus the `StepHandler` type both gained an optional `model` field so serialized generators can read the per-request model instead of closing over request-time state. This lets a thread grown on a large-window model get summarized down on the first step after a mid-thread model switch rather than being rejected forever.",
